Be Right Back (BRB) is a small Arexx script for the TransAmiga BBS that 
will allow your users to leave there terminal to take a break 
(i.e. to go to the bathroom, get a cup'o java, answer the door) and not 
have to worry about get logged off due to the dreaded USER INACTIVITY LOGOFF.

Installation is very simple. 

BRB.trans file to your BBS:Rexx directory
BRB.Ansi/BRB.txt files to your BBS:Text directory

then just add a line to your main.rx (or where ever) like this

B Be Right Back           20 -------- brb.trans 

(the above spacing is not exact)

Also, you can use ANY ANSI screen you want for the BRB screen, just rename it
to BRB.Ansi. (I used BBSDraw to save my BRB.ansi as a simple .txt file)

